      "reasoning": "Damage step.\n\
Then End Combat.\n\
Then Postcombat Main.\n\
Likely Ajani +1 or -2.\n\
If -2, they kill Otter.\n\
If they kill Otter, I have 1 Otter + 2 Slickshots.\n\
Slickshot 1 (9 power), Slickshot 2 (7 power).\n\
Otter (5 power).\n\
Total 21 damage.\n\
Still lethal.\n\
I allow it.\n\
Wait, I can save Otter with `Bounce Off`?\n\
\"Return target creature... to its owner's hand.\"\n\
Can I bounce MY creature?\n\
Yes, \"owner's hand\".\n\
If I bounce Otter, I can replay it next turn?\n\
No, it's a TOKEN. It dies if bounced.\n\
So `Bounce Off` kills my Token.\n\
Bad idea.\n\
Can `Into the Flood Maw` bounce my Token?\n\
\"Return target nonland permanent to its owner's hand. If you controlled... enter tapped.\"\n\
If I target my Token, it dies.\n\
So saving Token is impossible with Bounce.\n\
I have `Shock`?\n\
If they target Otter, I can Shock Ajani?\n\
He has 4 loyalty. -2 = 2 loyalty.\n\
Shock him = 0 loyalty. He dies.\n\
Otter still dies (ability on stack).\n\
But Ajani is gone.\n\
This is good.\n\
If they +1 (make Kithkin), Ajani goes to 5 loyalty.\n\
I Shock face? Or Ajani (3).\n\
Maybe Shock face is better. 7 -> 5.\n\
Then Slickshots only need 5 damage.\n\
With 2 Slickshots, I deal 5 easily.\n\
So I let them kill Otter if they want.\n\
Pass priority.\n\
\n\
Action: Pass to end turn.\n\
\n\
